course: dictionary
lesson: 2106
title: Opposites and turn-arounds
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: The word contrary means opposite, or very different from what came before. Look for it in the clues around it. «Bored? On the contrary, I loved it.» The speaker did not feel bored, because on the contrary turns the idea around.
explain: In Toad's story, people praise him, and he answers «Not at all!» or «On the contrary!» Toad is not agreeing with the praise. The phrase warns you that the opposite is coming, so read on to see what he really means.
explain: A contrary person deliberately does the opposite of what others want, said «con-TRAIR-ee». The nursery rhyme «Mary, Mary, quite contrary» describes a stubborn girl. Contrary to means against or different from, as in «contrary to the rules».
fact: Contrary means opposite or very different, as in «contrary opinions».
fact: «On the contrary» says that the opposite is true.
fact: A contrary person deliberately does the opposite of what others want, said «con-TRAIR-ee».
fact: «Contrary to» means against or different from, as in «contrary to the rules».
fact: Phrases to know: on the contrary, contrary to, to the contrary, evidence to the contrary.
exercise: «Bored? On the contrary, I loved it.» What does on the contrary tell you? | *The opposite is true | The speaker is asking a question | Something is being repeated | The speaker is tired
exercise: What does a contrary person deliberately do? | Always agrees with everyone | Sings loudly in class | Runs away from home | *Does the opposite of what others want
exercise: «The plan was contrary to the rules.» What does contrary to mean here? | Written on a sign | *Against the rules | Just like the rules | Following the rules exactly
test: Which phrase means the opposite is true? | Sooner or later | *On the contrary | Once upon a time | In the middle
test: Two people have contrary opinions. What does contrary mean? | Very loud | *Opposite or very different | The same as each other | Old and tired
exam: Toad replies «On the contrary!» when people praise him. What does this show? | He is agreeing with everyone | *He disagrees with the praise | He is leaving the room | He is falling asleep
